+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Some clients send partial updates as JSON Merge Patch documents, which are simpler than JSON Patch (RFC 6902). The toolkit can only apply RFC 6902 today, so services have to implement merge patch themselves.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add an exported `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` to `src/index.ts`. It returns the merged document and never mutates its inputs.
+- Governing standard: JSON Merge Patch, RFC 7396 §2 (the `MergePatch` algorithm). RFC 7396 obsoletes RFC 7386, which the request cites. The algorithm is the same, and the project config names 7396, so 7396 is cited.
+- Not breaking: this is a new export and existing behaviour is unchanged.
+- Out of scope: generating a merge patch from two documents, a content-type or HTTP layer, and any change to `applyPatch`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-merge-patch`: applying an RFC 7396 JSON Merge Patch to a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: new exported function. It reuses the existing private helpers `isObject`, `setMember` and `cloneJson`.
+- `test/merge-patch.test.ts`: new tests.
+- No new dependencies and no `package.json` change.
